00:04:34.647 --> 00:04:35.827
"I have really sweaty hands.

00:04:35.827 --> 00:04:38.370
"What causes it to really
sweat, and is it normal?"

00:04:38.370 --> 00:04:40.050
If you have really sweaty hands,

00:04:40.050 --> 00:04:43.370
that could be a condition
called palmar hyperhidrosis.

00:04:43.370 --> 00:04:44.960
Palmar meaning the palm of your hand,

00:04:44.960 --> 00:04:48.280
hyper meaning more of, hidrosis, sweating.

00:04:48.280 --> 00:04:50.230
This isn't that of an unusual condition,

00:04:50.230 --> 00:04:51.830
but it causes a lot of distress to people

00:04:51.830 --> 00:04:53.910
'cause when you're shaking
peoples' hands, interacting,

00:04:53.910 --> 00:04:55.470
it's obviously very uncomfortable.

00:04:55.470 --> 00:04:58.560
Treatments for this
usually are antiperspirant,

00:04:58.560 --> 00:05:00.040
like the thing we use under our arms,

00:05:00.040 --> 00:05:01.930
but here to plug those sweat glands.

00:05:01.930 --> 00:05:02.850
The glands that are found here

00:05:02.850 --> 00:05:04.680
are mostly eccrine sweat glands.

00:05:04.680 --> 00:05:07.680
Which start sweating not to
thermoregulate your body,

00:05:07.680 --> 00:05:10.730
to cool you off, but really
as a result of nervousness.

00:05:10.730 --> 00:05:12.230
You have this sympathetic nervous system

00:05:12.230 --> 00:05:14.710
which is your fight or flight
response nervous system.

00:05:14.710 --> 00:05:16.420
That's what happens when you see a lion,

00:05:16.420 --> 00:05:17.770
when you're about to give a speech,

00:05:17.770 --> 00:05:19.260
when you're arguing with your partner.

00:05:19.260 --> 00:05:20.410
That's why your hands sweat.

00:05:20.410 --> 00:05:23.770
As a result, those sweat glands
start releasing that fluid.

00:05:23.770 --> 00:05:25.210
Now, when you put antiperspirant on,

00:05:25.210 --> 00:05:26.720
you essentially block those ducts,

00:05:26.720 --> 00:05:28.480
no fluid gets released, you sweat less.

00:05:28.480 --> 00:05:29.620
Sometimes they don't work.

00:05:29.620 --> 00:05:31.670
You can use clinical strength products.

00:05:31.670 --> 00:05:34.430
If that fails, there's
always Botox injections.

00:05:34.430 --> 00:05:36.340
Yeah, you could actually inject Botox

00:05:36.340 --> 00:05:38.250
into the sweat glands of your palm

00:05:38.250 --> 00:05:39.550
to reduce that sweating.

00:05:39.550 --> 00:05:40.870
It works really well.

00:05:40.870 --> 00:05:42.690
I've had some doctors talk to me about it

00:05:42.690 --> 00:05:45.420
'cause I have underarm
sweating that's pretty bad.

00:05:45.420 --> 00:05:47.140
And I might be doing that in the future.

00:05:47.140 --> 00:05:51.080
In fact, if you want me to
make a Botox sweating video

00:05:51.080 --> 00:05:54.460
injection into me, God I
couldn't phrase it any worse,

00:05:54.460 --> 00:05:55.660
leave it down below in the comments.

00:05:55.660 --> 00:05:58.370
I want to make videos at least a series

00:05:58.370 --> 00:06:01.400
of different medical procedures
being performed on me.

00:06:01.400 --> 00:06:03.550
If you're game, hit me in the comments.

00:06:03.550 --> 00:06:07.420
Jude Bratton "What eyesight
does require glasses?"

00:06:07.420 --> 00:06:09.510
I think you mean like
what should my eyesight be

00:06:09.510 --> 00:06:11.110
that I would need glasses?

00:06:11.110 --> 00:06:12.880
Well, glasses are important.

00:06:12.880 --> 00:06:14.060
First of all, I wear them.

00:06:14.060 --> 00:06:14.940
They could help with issues

00:06:14.940 --> 00:06:16.900
like farsightedness, nearsightedness.

00:06:16.900 --> 00:06:19.220
The ideal vision that
many professions require

00:06:19.220 --> 00:06:22.510
is 20/20 vision which means
that you can see an eye chart

00:06:22.510 --> 00:06:25.725
from 20 feet away as well as
a person with normal vision

00:06:25.725 --> 00:06:27.640
can see from 20 feet away.

00:06:27.640 --> 00:06:30.850
If you have 20/30 vision,
that means you can see

00:06:30.850 --> 00:06:34.000
from 20 feet what they
can see from 30 feet away.

00:06:34.000 --> 00:06:35.150
Meaning someone with normal vision

00:06:35.150 --> 00:06:36.340
can see better than you.

00:06:36.340 --> 00:06:38.320
So 20/30 is worse than 20/20.

00:06:38.320 --> 00:06:39.710
There's no rules for this.

00:06:39.710 --> 00:06:42.560
If you have 20/30 vision, 20/40 vision,

00:06:42.560 --> 00:06:44.740
you may have that in
one eye, in both eyes.

00:06:44.740 --> 00:06:46.770
You need to have a conversation
with your optometrist

00:06:46.770 --> 00:06:47.660
or ophthalmologist.

00:06:47.660 --> 00:06:51.610
Some cases where you need
perfect vision for your job,

00:06:51.610 --> 00:06:53.650
it's important to correct
your vision early on.

00:06:53.650 --> 00:06:55.650
In some other instances
where it's not a big deal

00:06:55.650 --> 00:06:57.310
and you're sitting in front of a computer,

00:06:57.310 --> 00:06:59.390
it might not be so important for you.

00:06:59.390 --> 00:07:01.900
I will say that if your
vision is chronically bad

00:07:01.900 --> 00:07:03.820
and you're squinting and you're straining,

00:07:03.820 --> 00:07:06.600
that can cause headaches,
irritation of your eyes,

00:07:06.600 --> 00:07:07.630
all sorts of issues.

00:07:07.630 --> 00:07:10.560
So I do recommend you go
get your eyes checked.

00:07:10.560 --> 00:07:12.310
That's part of being a healthy person.

